Simplest: in fetch requests add `headers: { connection: 'close' }`? Undici may ignore. Better: after close callback, call server.closeAllConnections(). Actually `server.close()` stops accepting new connections and waits for existing. Call `server.closeAllConnections()` right after `server.close()`.

Let me update `withServer`:
```js
await new Promise((resolve) => {
  server.close(resolve);
  server.closeAllConnections();
});
```

This makes tests fast. Let me also reduce duplicated fetch? Not necessary.

